<BaseLayout title="Respiratory device manufacturers in India" description="How to verify a respiratory device manufacturer, its licence and country of manufacture in India, with a sourced Home Medix profile.">
  <article class="prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Manufacturers', href: '/manufacturers/' }]} />
    <h1>Respiratory device manufacturers in India</h1>
    <p class="lead">A manufacturer’s identity, a brand name and a local seller are different facts. Check the documents for the exact device before describing it as made in India.</p>

    <h2>Manufacturer profile</h2>
    <p><a href="/manufacturers/home-medix/">Home Medix</a> — a Bengaluru-based respiratory and home-care brand that describes itself as a manufacturer. The profile separates its published claims from model-specific evidence still to be checked.</p>

    <h2>How to verify origin and responsibility</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Check the device label and current manual for the legal manufacturer, manufacturing address, model and country of manufacture. A brand or Indian business address alone does not establish where a unit was made.</li>
      <li>Ask for the applicable manufacturing or import licence and its model or device scope. Match the legal entity, site and product to the documentation; a general certification does not establish origin for every model.</li>
      <li>Identify the importer, distributor and seller where applicable, and confirm who handles installation, warranty and service at your location.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>For product comparisons, see the <a href="/top-5/indian-made-oxygen-concentrators/">Indian-made oxygen concentrators guide</a> and verify the current label and documents for the unit offered.</p>
    <p><strong>Recommendation:</strong> request the model-specific label and licence before relying on a country-of-origin or manufacturer claim.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
